---
/**
 * Privacy. Must keep describing the real posture: region-split GA4 (opt-in gate in the EEA/UK/CH, notice plus opt-out elsewhere, per src/scripts/consent.ts), same-origin assets, mailto contact, Cloudflare Worker hosting. A change to the consent flow that does not reach this page publishes a false statement about what the site does.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const EMAIL = 'mehtadpratik@gmail.com';
import { siteOrigin, breadcrumb } from '../lib/schema';

// Depth-1 breadcrumb, matching /about. The child pages under /work and /journal already emit trails that point here, so the parents should exist as crumbs too.
const bcOrigin = siteOrigin(Astro.site);
const schema = [breadcrumb(bcOrigin, [{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy' }])];

---

<Base
  schema={schema}
  title="Privacy Policy | Pratik Mehta"
  description="What limited data mehtapratik.com collects, and how it is used. Analytics are opt-in in Europe and opt-out everywhere else, and every asset is self-hosted."
  activeNav=""
>
  <section class="legal">
    <header class="rev-load">
      <div class="page-kicker">[ Privacy ]</div>
      <h1 class="page-h1">Privacy Policy.</h1>
      <div class="updated">Last updated 28 July 2026</div>
    </header>

    <div class="prose rev">
      <p>This is the personal portfolio of Pratik Mehta. It collects very little, and this page explains what and why.</p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>The site uses Google Analytics 4 to understand general traffic: which pages are viewed, rough location, device and browser, and how visitors arrive. How it loads depends on where you are.</p>
      <p>In the EEA, the UK, and Switzerland it is <strong>off until you accept</strong> the cookie notice. If you decline, no analytics run and no analytics cookies are set. Everywhere else it runs when the page loads, and the notice says so and gives you a one-click opt out. Either way the choice is yours to change at any time, and declining or opting out is remembered on your device.</p>
      <p>I read these analytics as aggregate reports. The data is never sold, and it is never used for advertising.</p>
      {/* [NEEDS: the property's actual Data Retention value, GA4 Admin -> Data settings -> Data retention. It is 2 or 14 months; state the real one here rather than describing retention in the abstract.] */}
      <p>Google processes this data on my behalf as a service provider, and may store and process it outside your country, including in the United States. Rough location is derived from your IP address by Google; I never see or store the address itself. Event-level data expires on the retention period set for the property, after which only aggregate reporting remains.</p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>The only cookies this site sets are Google Analytics cookies. There are no advertising or cross-site tracking cookies, and ad personalization is switched off in the tag itself rather than left to a setting. If you opt out after analytics have loaded, the cookies already set are expired immediately. Fonts are self-hosted and served from this domain, so no third-party font service receives your data.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>The contact page opens your own email client and sends a message directly to me. There is no form and nothing is stored on a server. Anything you choose to include, such as your name and message, reaches me by email and is used only to reply.</p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>The site runs on Cloudflare, served by a Cloudflare Worker at the edge. Images, video, and fonts are served from this same domain. Like any host, Cloudflare may process standard request and security logs, including IP addresses, to deliver and protect the site. That happens whether or not you accept analytics, and is separate from it.</p>
      <p>Cloudflare also reports which country a request came from, which is how the notice above knows which version to show you. That check happens at the edge, before any analytics load, and the answer is used for nothing else.</p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>You can accept or decline analytics at any time with the <strong>Cookies</strong> control in the footer. The concept demos have no footer, so when analytics are running there they carry their own one-click control at the foot of the page instead. Either one applies everywhere on this domain, and you can clear cookies through your browser. Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  /* type tiers — family/weight/tracking only; rules below set size + color */
  .prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--t-h3-font); font-weight: var(--t-h3-weight); letter-spacing: var(--t-h3-track);
  }
  .legal .updated {
    font-family: var(--t-label-font); font-weight: var(--t-label-weight); letter-spacing: var(--t-label-track);
  }


  .legal { padding: var(--space-4xl) 0 var(--space-4xl); }
  .legal .updated { font-size: var(--fs-2xs); text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: var(--space-lg); }
  /* measure, paragraph type and bold all come from global .prose */
  .prose { margin-top: var(--space-2xl); }
  .prose h2 { font-size: var(--fs-xl); color: var(--text); margin: var(--space-xl) 0 var(--space-sm); }
  .prose a { color: var(--accent-text); text-decoration: underline; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .legal { padding: var(--space-3xl) 0 var(--space-3xl); } }
</style>
